      "id": "source-6",
      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "Claude Opus 5",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-25T11:00:00Z",
      "note": "The attacker EOA sent 20 Gnosis transactions; three reach the exploit contract, at blocks 21120283, 21120284 and 21120285. The first touches the pool but nets nothing, the second is the drain, and the third only forwards 567.98 WETH from the exploit contract to the EOA, so the v1 anchor is the earliest suitable one and is kept. The pool proxy emitted no Upgraded event before the exploit and its EIP-1967 slot goes from zero at block 15927424 to 0x2d5bc0f897ad211ef9f954eadf59c43fb1ec4788 at its creation block 15927425 and holds it through block 21120283, so the exploited implementation is 312.0 days old. The proxy was created by the Aave-fork configurator factory 0xa91b9095efa6c0568467562032202108e49c9ef8, sent by 0x79c815a50f2f0cb91772945d94fc65371f5d9881, neither of which is an attacker address. Loss is the attacker-side net gain of underlyings across the two pool-touching transactions; the matching debt tokens were never repaid. This is the same ERC-677 reentrancy class as the Hundred Finance Gnosis incident of the same day, but a different fork and a different code hash, so it carries its own failure identity."
    }
  ],
